169
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:47,080
In computer science, bigger notation describes how an algorithm scales.

170
00:09:47,700 --> 00:09:52,600
O of one means the operation takes a constant amount of time, regardless of how much data you throw at it.

171
00:09:52,660 --> 00:09:54,240
