00:09:57,100 --> 00:10:05,440
And to make marine look revolutionary, they contrast this with a fast Fourier transform, or FFT, which is a standard way of processing signals.

175
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:15,180
They point out that an FFT operates at O of n log n complexity per block, meaning it slows down significantly as the data block gets larger.

176
00:10:15,340 --> 00:10:15,520
Right.

177
00:10:15,560 --> 00:10:17,380
It takes more time the more data there is.

